Twin structure: row 0 of S_tower is all-ones at every order (verified above as
normalize no-op), so core T_{2^k-1} vertex v (1..2^k-1) carries the BINARY index
of the tower: twins at the last doubling are (v, v+2^(k-1)); vertex 2^(k-1) is the
border's twin.
VERDICT on "Walsh plus low-weight correction": REFUTED in the entrywise sense —
nnz(C_N) = N^2/2 exactly (HALF of all entries differ; the naive N log2 N recursion
argument fails because the -2I/+2I corrections cancel/seed on diagonals).
PARTIAL in the spectral sense: every row of S_tower has |<row, some Walsh char>| >= N/2;
per-row max|dot| histogram is the exact ladder {N/2: 4 rows, N/2+4: 8, ..., N-4: 8, N: 4};
diagonal dot spectrum = full arithmetic progression -N..N step 4, each value x2 (+-N x1).

